---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TaxCalculator from '../../components/TaxCalculator.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/Contact.astro'; // Assuming there is a CTA or Contact component. We'll check later.
---

<Layout 
  title="Greece 50% Tax Break Calculator (Article 5C) | Taxomade"
  description="Calculate your exact tax savings with the Greek Article 5C tax incentive. Find out how much you can save on your income tax by moving to Greece."
  image="/images/guides/tax_break_hero.png"
>
  <main class="pt-24 pb-16 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <!-- Hero Section -->
      <div class="text-center mb-12">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide uppercase mb-4">
          Article 5C Calculator
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-6 tracking-tight">Calculate Your <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-600 to-indigo-600">50% Tax Break</span></h1>
        <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-slate-600 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          Greece offers one of the most generous tax incentives in Europe. Enter your gross annual income below to see exactly how much you can save under the Article 5C regime.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- The Calculator -->
      <TaxCalculator />
      
      <!-- Educational Content -->
      <div class="mt-16 prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-bold prose-a:text-blue-600">
        <h2>How the 50% Tax Exemption Works</h2>
        <p>
          The Greek government introduced Article 5C of the Income Tax Code to attract foreign talent, remote workers, and digital nomads (with specific visas). Under this regime, <strong>50% of your Greek-sourced employment or freelance income is completely exempt from income tax</strong> and the special solidarity contribution for up to seven consecutive years.
        </p>
        
        <h3>Who is eligible?</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>You must not have been a Greek tax resident for 5 of the past 6 years.</li>
          <li>You must transfer your tax residency from an EU/EEA state or a country with a tax cooperation agreement with Greece.</li>
          <li>You must start new employment in Greece or set up a new sole proprietorship (freelance business) in Greece.</li>
          <li>You must declare your intent to stay in Greece for at least two years.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-600 p-4 my-6 rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-sm text-blue-800 m-0 font-medium">
            <strong>Important Note on Digital Nomad Visas:</strong> If you are a Non-EU citizen planning to use the Digital Nomad Visa (DNV), you are generally <em>not eligible</em> for this tax break, as the DNV prohibits you from entering the Greek labor market or setting up a local freelance business. EU citizens can apply easily.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h3>How the math works</h3>
        <p>
          The standard Greek income tax is progressive, scaling from 9% up to 44%. If you earn €60,000, you are normally taxed on the full €60,000, pushing a large chunk of your income into the 44% bracket. 
        </p>
        <p>
          Under Article 5C, you are only taxed on €30,000. This not only halves your taxable base but also keeps your income entirely out of the highest tax brackets, resulting in a dramatically lower effective tax rate.
        </p>
        
        <p class="mt-8">
          <a href="/guides/50-percent-tax-break-article-5c">Read the full guide on Article 5C here &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
